# NOTICE — credits and attributions

This project is the official release face for **ffx-mod-hooks**, the runtime
engine hook layer for FINAL FANTASY X/X-2 HD Remaster. The binaries are built
from source maintained in a private repo during beta.

## Libraries linked in the binaries

- **PolyHook2** — Stephen Eckels (stevemk14ebr) — https://github.com/stevemk14ebr/PolyHook_2_0
  - License: MIT
  - x86 detour engine used across the hook layer.
- **MinHook** — Tsuda Kageyu — https://github.com/TsudaKageyu/minhook
  - License: BSD-2-Clause
  - Used by F7InLive for read-only battle hooks.
- **Zydis / Zycore** — zyantific — https://github.com/zyantific/zydis
  - License: MIT
  - Static dependency of PolyHook2.
- **asmjit / asmtk** — https://github.com/asmjit/asmjit
  - License: zlib
  - Static dependency of PolyHook2.
- **Xe.BinaryMapper** — Luciano Ciccariello (Xeeynamo) — https://github.com/xeeynamo/Xe.BinaryMapper
  - License: MIT
  - Binary struct mapper used by the SIN injector tooling.

## Community techniques

- **FFX module loader / DINPUT8 proxy** (`dinput8.dll` → `modules\*.dll`) — ffgriever
  - https://github.com/ffgriever — the standard FFX HD modding loading path.
- **DINPUT8 main-thread seam** (`IDirectInputDevice8::GetDeviceState` vtable
  slot 9) — discovered and proven in-house by the FFX Mod Studio project
  (2026-06-03) as the race-free main-thread bridge.

## Our own code

- All hook implementations, the probe, the SIN injector, the menu shell and
  the photo mode actions were developed by the FFX Mod Studio project.
- The RVA address ledger (`ffx_addresses.h`) was built from our own IDA Pro
  reverse engineering.

